## Goal
Make `scripts/install.sh` never delete a build directory that the caller supplied, as found in cross-review.

## Problems
None. The previous cleanup deleted any directory whose path matched `*/portero-build.*`. That included a caller-provided directory with such a name.

## Decision
`rmbuild` in `scripts/install.sh` now returns immediately when `PORTERO_BUILD_DIR` is set. Only a directory that `build-app.sh` created itself with `mktemp` (no `PORTERO_BUILD_DIR` given) is removed. The name pattern check stays as a second guard for that case. Ownership is decided by who chose the directory, not by what it is called, because a name can be matched by accident or on purpose.

The dry-run output follows the same rule: "would remove" is printed only when the script would actually remove the directory.

`scripts/test-install.sh` gets a regression test. It creates a caller-chosen directory named like a temp one (`portero-build.mine`) and puts a marker file in it. It runs a dry-run install with `PORTERO_BUILD_DIR` pointing at it, then checks that the marker is still there.

